('50', '2', 'Paragraph about Napoleon', '<p>Napoleon Bonaparte, the renowned French military leader and emperor, rose to power during the tumultuous period of the French Revolution. Known for his strategic brilliance and charismatic leadership, Napoleon quickly became a prominent figure in European history. His military conquests, such as the Battle of Austerlitz and the Battle of Waterloo, solidified his reputation as a formidable commander. However, Napoleon''s legacy is not solely defined by his military achievements; his innovative legal reforms, known as the Napoleonic Code, significantly influenced legal systems worldwide. Despite his accomplishments, Napoleon''s ambitious pursuit of power ultimately led to his downfall. His failed invasion of Russia and eventual defeat at Waterloo marked the end of his reign and exile to the remote island of Saint Helena. Napoleon''s complex character and legacy continue to spark debate among historians and scholars, with some viewing him as a visionary leader who modernized Europe, while others criticize his authoritarian tendencies and expansionist policies. Overall, Napoleon''s impact on European history remains profound, leaving a lasting legacy that continues to be studied and debated to this day.</p>', 'text', 'completed', 'private', NULL, NULL, '0.00', '2025-09-29 09:36:21', '2025-09-29 09:36:54', NULL, NULL, NULL),
